WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.810 --> 00:00:03.660
- [Reporter] Smoke
plumes, a collapsed tower

00:00:03.660 --> 00:00:05.550
and destroyed military equipment.

00:00:05.550 --> 00:00:07.860
These satellite images
from private providers

00:00:07.860 --> 00:00:09.870
appear to show a string
of Ukrainian attacks

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.880
on Snake Island in the Black Sea

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.800
just before Russia
announced it was withdrawing

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:15.113
from the territory.

00:00:15.113 --> 00:00:19.113
(man speaking foreign language)

00:00:22.649 --> 00:00:24.810
The territory sits in a strategic position

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:27.240
for both countries, Russia seized it

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.710
and appeared to fortify the island

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.900
to use it as a base in the Black Sea,

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.670
threatening targets on Ukraine's shores

00:00:32.670 --> 00:00:36.450
and watching the ports of
Odesa, blocking grain exports.

00:00:36.450 --> 00:00:39.300
For Ukraine the territory has
become a symbol of resistance

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:41.520
after the recording of
an obscene radio message

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:44.154
sent by border guards to
the invaders went viral.

00:00:44.154 --> 00:00:46.560
(man speaking foreign language)

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:49.080
Since then Kyiv put the
island on postage stamps

00:00:49.080 --> 00:00:51.180
and publicized its
military operations there

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:54.120
in highly edited footage
posted on social media.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.190
After a number of attacks,
Ukraine said it was able

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:59.220
to claim it back, also,
thanks to foreign weapons.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:00.630
Here's how the small island

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:02.943
came to play an outsized role in the war.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:07.740
On the first day of Russia's
invasion in late February

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.190
it sees Snake Island with
help from its Moskva warship.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.800
This satellite image shows
the territory before the war

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:16.650
when it hosted a garrison of
Ukrainian border guardsmen.

00:01:16.650 --> 00:01:18.690
Moskva moved towards the territory as part

00:01:18.690 --> 00:01:22.650
of a wider strategy to control
the Black Sea, analysts say.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:24.630
But keeping control of
it became a priority

00:01:24.630 --> 00:01:26.100
when the Moskva was taken down

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:29.010
by a pair of Ukrainian
missiles on April 14th.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:32.250
These images show the ship
just days before it was struck.

00:01:32.250 --> 00:01:34.110
The vessel, considered one of Moskva's

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.840
most powerful warships, was
being used off the coast

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.220
of Odesa to provide air

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:40.470
and sea capability to Russia's fleet.

00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.290
The striking of Moskva was
proof of Ukraine's ability

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.300
to hit targets in the area and resulted

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:48.120
in other Russian vessels
moving further offshore.

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:50.010
- Owning an island like this

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:52.230
and being able to put long
range air defense systems

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:56.760
on it is a way of sort
of covering that loss.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:01:57.930
- [Reporter] That's Thomas Bullock,

00:01:57.930 --> 00:02:00.660
an open source intelligence
analyst who specializes

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.120
in tracking and monitoring
the Russian military.

00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.010
- Other vessels in the Black Sea fleet

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:06.540
do have an air defense capability

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:08.193
but it's more limited in range.

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.250
- [Reporter] As the territory
became a focus for Russia,

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.110
Kyiv began striking back.

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.510
In May the Ukrainian
military release footage

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.660
that it said showed a strike
on a Russian helicopter.

00:02:18.660 --> 00:02:20.370
Days later, Ukraine said a drone strike

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:23.280
hit more Russian targets on Snake Island.

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:25.830
Kyiv used weapons, such
as a TB2 Bayraktar,

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:29.070
a type of unmanned drone
and the SU27 fighter jet

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:31.710
to inflict significant
damage on Russian forces,

00:02:31.710 --> 00:02:33.300
but it wasn't enough to dislodge them,

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:35.070
defense experts say.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:37.650
- They attacked set the
island multiple times,

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:41.730
striking it with TB2
Bayraktar, attacking boats,

00:02:41.730 --> 00:02:43.080
circling around the island

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.500
and then finally leveling all
of the buildings on the island

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:49.770
with an air strike from manned SU27s.

00:02:49.770 --> 00:02:51.780
- [Reporter] Those strikes
appeared to damage structures

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:52.860
on the territory.

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.360
Weeks later, they were fortified

00:02:54.360 --> 00:02:57.570
and Moskva put additional
defenses in place.

00:02:57.570 --> 00:02:59.760
Analysts say comparison satellite images

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.790
from May 12th and June 5th
shows that in a matter of weeks

00:03:02.790 --> 00:03:04.620
new tent structures have been erected

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:07.710
and additional panser and tore
anti-aircraft missile systems

00:03:07.710 --> 00:03:09.030
have been put in place.

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.030
- [Thomas] So, we see a
large number of trenches

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:14.670
that have been dug to protect
vehicles from the sides.

00:03:14.670 --> 00:03:19.080
So, it's sort of limits
even air attack capabilities

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.080
to a certain extent.

00:03:21.270 --> 00:03:22.800
- [Reporter] But, those
additional entrenchments

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:24.480
did not stop Ukraine from continuing

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:26.907
to bombard Russian forces on Snake Island.

00:03:26.907 --> 00:03:29.430
The Ukrainian military
released edited footage

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.560
that it said showed air
strikes on the territory

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.210
on June 21st.

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.880
The Russian Defense Ministry
said it had repelled attacks

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.500
on the same day.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.470
Compared to a few days earlier,
patches of burnt vegetation

00:03:40.470 --> 00:03:43.230
and a collapsed tower
were captured in images.

00:03:43.230 --> 00:03:45.390
A week later, short range missile systems

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.850
appeared to be damaged by Kyiv's forces.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.130
Ukraine's military
commander posted a video

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:53.220
appearing to show a Ukrainian
self-propelled Howitzer,

00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.690
an artillery weapon with a range

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:57.660
of more than 25 miles,
striking the island.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:04:00.780
He also thanked foreign
partners for weapons assistance.

00:04:00.780 --> 00:04:03.090
The most recent attacks
coincided with the arrival

00:04:03.090 --> 00:04:05.220
in Ukraine of new long range weapons,

00:04:05.220 --> 00:04:06.990
high mars and harpoon missiles,

00:04:06.990 --> 00:04:09.330
sent by the US and its allies.

00:04:09.330 --> 00:04:11.970
There's no indication that
Ukraine used those weapons

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:14.640
on Snake Island, but analysts
say the delivery itself

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:17.490
could have been a factor in
Russia's decision to retreat.

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.510
Russia didn't immediately
respond to a request for comment.

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:24.780
Ukraine declined to comment on
whether newly sent US weapons

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:26.163
were used in the strikes.

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.970
The contest over Snake Island
is one battle that played out

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:32.370
in the wider war in Ukraine
where equipment losses

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:34.140
and casualties are mounting.

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:36.360
- The levels of equipment
loss we're seeing

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:38.047
and the manpower losses we're seeing,

00:04:38.047 --> 00:04:39.750
it's just it's fractional compared

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:41.430
to places like the Donbass.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:43.260
- [Reporter] Moskav's
troops are pushing to expand

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:44.760
and consolidate areas they hold

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:47.520
across large parts of Eastern Ukraine.

00:04:47.520 --> 00:04:49.170
Moskva has steadily gained ground

00:04:49.170 --> 00:04:51.990
by using its advantage of
heavy weapons, analysts say.

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:54.660
Still, the loss of Snake
Island is a strategic blow

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:56.073
as the war grinds on.

